{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And Abram pitched, and came and dwelt.</b> It should have written 'and Abram came and pitched and dwelt.' Rather, <b>ויאהל</b> here is not the language of setting up a tent, but the language of taking down a tent. There are many words in the holy language written in one form that have two meanings, one the opposite of the other — for example, והרים את הדשן (removing the ashes) and עשית סירותיו לדשנו (you shall make its pans for its ashes), and many more. So too here, <b>ויאהל</b> — in the vernacular, 'desplanter' in Old French — that is to say, he uprooted his tent from its first encampment, which was in the land of Canaan, and pitched it at Elonei Mamre."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:08.466867620Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}